  "WinboxName": "Cleaned windows",
  "WinboxDescription": "this example demonstrates the ability to cut out most of the junk from Windows. This example is for use on a desktop where you want to get the cleanest possible build of windows. THIS IS NOT AN EMBEDDED ASSEMBLY IN ITS PURE FORM! you can use it as a template for embedded to reduce the space occupied by the system on the embedded device, but do not forget to change \u0022app\u003Elaunch\u0022 to \u0022launch instead of desktop\u0022. however, for embedded, I recommend simply applying the \u0022removing Windows/System apps\u0022 patch, which will remove almost the entire UX of windows at once, but your shell (if it is not UWP) will work.",
